course: dictionary
lesson: 2103
title: Contractions
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A contraction is a short form made by joining two words into one, with an apostrophe (') where letters have been left out. «Don't» is a contraction of do not: the o in not is missing, and the apostrophe takes its place.
explain: Look at «I'm going to the park.» I'm is short for I am, so the apostrophe shows that the a has gone. To check a contraction, say the two full words in your head and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Contractions sound like talking, so you will find them in stories, diaries and chatty messages. «I can't find my PE kit» sounds natural. In very formal writing, such as a letter to the council, write the full words instead.
fact: Contraction is a noun. It comes from the verb contract, which means to make smaller or shorter.
fact: A contraction squeezes two words into one with an apostrophe, like could've for could have.
fact: An apostrophe shows where letters are missing: don't (do not), can't (cannot), I'm (I am), we're (we are).
fact: In science, a contraction means getting smaller or shorter: metals contract when they cool, and muscles contract to pull bones.
fact: Contractions are not used in very formal writing, so write «cannot» instead of «can't» in a school report.
exercise: What is the contraction for «do not»? | *don't | do'nt | do't | dont
exercise: «I'm going to the shop now.» What two words is I'm short for? | I do | I will | *I am | I have
exercise: Which sentence is best for a formal letter to the council? | Yeah, we're cool with it | Hey, we can't wait to see you! | Can't wait, see you there! | *We cannot wait to see you.
test: In «they're», which letters have been left out? | the t from they | the whole word they | *the a from are | the h from they
test: In science, a metal gets smaller when it cools. What is this called? | *contraction | multiplication | addition | expansion
exam: Which is the correct contraction of «you are»? | youre | *you're | yo'u're | your
